What is a DeNOx Catalyst?
DeNOx catalysts are specialized chemical substances engineered to selectively reduce nitrogen oxides (NOx) through targeted catalytic reactions, primarily employing reducing agents such as ammonia (NH3) or urea. These catalysts serve as the functional core of Selective Catalytic Reduction (SCR) systems-an industry-leading emission control technology that converts harmful NOx compounds into harmless nitrogen (N2) and water vapor. SCR systems equipped with DeNOx catalysts are widely deployed across an extensive range of industries, including power plants, cement factories, petroleum refineries, steel mills, and the transportation sector, all of which face mounting pressure to comply with increasingly rigorous air quality standards worldwide.
